        <p class="profile-detail-region">City · Central &amp; East Asia</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Chang'an</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">202 BCE – 904 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bang">Liu Bang</a>, the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a>, made it his capital after 202 BCE, moving his court to the Changle Palace in 200 BCE; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui</a> built a new city, Daxing, in 582, which was renamed Chang’an in 618.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guanzhong">Guanzhong</a> region along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wei-river">Wei River</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaanxi">Shaanxi</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>; the Han city lay about 5 km north-west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xian">Xi’an</a> of the Ming and Qing, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui</a> and Tang city south-east of it.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">Capital of the Western Han, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui</a> and Tang; the Weiyang Palace; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a>’s eastern end; a grid of walled wards and two great markets; Sogdian, Persian and other foreign communities; the model for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nara">Nara</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a>; the destruction of 904</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">The site lies within the modern city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xian">Xi’an</a>, whose walls the Ming built around the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui</a> and Tang palace district.</span></div>
